01:01:22.560 --> 01:01:26.520
from things I had created in prison

01:01:26.560 --> 01:01:31.560
to kind of frame them in certain ways

01:01:32.680 --> 01:01:37.680
to find some closure from all of that experience

01:01:38.320 --> 01:01:43.320
and create pieces that express how I'm feeling now.

01:01:44.600 --> 01:01:47.400
That sounds like an artist to me,

01:01:47.400 --> 01:01:50.280
because just even thinking about resin,

01:01:50.280 --> 01:01:53.320
I mean, when you said that I was like, of course,

01:01:53.320 --> 01:01:56.080
I would never think of doing that,

01:01:56.080 --> 01:01:58.760
but once you mentioned it, it makes so much sense

01:01:58.760 --> 01:01:59.920
because there's beauty in that.

01:01:59.920 --> 01:02:02.960
What did you, how did you find out about this side

01:02:02.960 --> 01:02:06.080
of reality and how did you work to get this

01:02:06.080 --> 01:02:07.760
as part of the documentary?

01:02:07.760 --> 01:02:09.040
Because it's so strong.

01:02:10.120 --> 01:02:13.280
Yeah, it is a big part and we realized,

01:02:13.280 --> 01:02:18.280
Maxine and I, when we didn't get access to reality

01:02:19.000 --> 01:02:21.680
and we knew this might not be the case

01:02:21.680 --> 01:02:24.880
that we really wanted to make this film about her

01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:29.880
and include her humor and her art and her words and poetry.

01:02:31.440 --> 01:02:35.480
And it just, this is a selection in the film

01:02:35.480 --> 01:02:39.120
of all these letters she was writing to her family

01:02:39.120 --> 01:02:41.720
and supporters and people were just collecting them

01:02:41.720 --> 01:02:44.040
and posting them on social media.

01:02:44.040 --> 01:02:47.600
And then you go back and you see the diary entries

01:02:47.600 --> 01:02:51.320
that are similar and also, so one of the reasons

01:02:51.320 --> 01:02:56.040
was to really insert reality into the film.

01:02:56.040 --> 01:02:57.900
But the second reason was because,

01:02:59.040 --> 01:03:03.640
was that her social media, her diary entries,

01:03:03.640 --> 01:03:07.160
but also her communication with her sister

01:03:07.160 --> 01:03:12.160
became such a big part of the pre-trial hearings

01:03:14.880 --> 01:03:19.640
and they were cherry picking all this information

01:03:19.760 --> 01:03:23.480
that for me is one of the most important parts of the film

01:03:23.480 --> 01:03:27.480
that I think should also resonate with the wide public,

01:03:27.480 --> 01:03:32.480
honestly across the world because that is what can happen

01:03:32.480 --> 01:03:36.920
when you have mass data, number one surveillance,

01:03:36.920 --> 01:03:39.600
but also mass data collection and storage,

01:03:39.600 --> 01:03:44.600
it's all there, the Facebook message conversation

01:03:44.840 --> 01:03:49.120
that predates reality's arrest.

01:03:49.160 --> 01:03:51.280
And I could tell in this audience

01:03:51.280 --> 01:03:56.000
that this audience did understand reality's humor

01:03:56.000 --> 01:03:57.960
better than the prosecutor.

01:03:59.800 --> 01:04:03.280
But I remember in the courtroom or even when you saw

01:04:03.280 --> 01:04:06.640
some of these TV clips that we were using

01:04:06.640 --> 01:04:10.560
that people were taking it so seriously and out of context

01:04:10.560 --> 01:04:14.840
and the prosecutor quoting one sentence

01:04:14.840 --> 01:04:18.040
or one part of a diary entry.

01:04:18.040 --> 01:04:21.200
And is this really the world we want to live in

01:04:21.200 --> 01:04:26.200
where we have to censor our personal conversations

01:04:26.240 --> 01:04:30.120
in a pandemic that's all digital with our friends

01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:34.560
and families and loved ones or even our diary entries

01:04:34.560 --> 01:04:37.200
that we think about what to put in our diary

01:04:37.200 --> 01:04:39.360
and like in our diaries.

01:04:39.360 --> 01:04:44.360
So this is where for me, reality's case

01:04:44.680 --> 01:04:47.480
expands so much beyond whistleblowing

01:04:47.480 --> 01:04:52.480
but also really is a case study on where things,

01:04:53.680 --> 01:04:57.400
not are just headed but actually are at right now

01:04:57.400 --> 01:05:01.600
where all this data is available and it doesn't have to be,

01:05:02.720 --> 01:05:07.720
it doesn't have to be you but it can also be the people

01:05:08.040 --> 01:05:12.160
who you love, your family members who all of a sudden

01:05:12.160 --> 01:05:16.720
do something that speak out against something

01:05:16.760 --> 01:05:19.440
that your government doesn't like

01:05:19.440 --> 01:05:22.640
and then all your private conversations

01:05:22.640 --> 01:05:27.640
are part of in this case a court case.

01:05:30.040 --> 01:05:31.800
I'd like to turn to the audience

01:05:31.800 --> 01:05:34.280
and see if we have some questions here

01:05:34.280 --> 01:05:37.920
and I gather somebody's watching if there's questions online

01:05:37.920 --> 01:05:40.200
and I have no idea how helpful I did about them

01:05:40.200 --> 01:05:45.040
but are there any questions that people have

01:05:45.040 --> 01:05:45.880
from the audience?

01:05:45.880 --> 01:05:47.440
Because I know I can keep going

01:05:47.440 --> 01:05:49.080
but I'd love to give you a chance.

01:05:50.120 --> 01:05:51.680
Yes.

01:05:51.680 --> 01:05:53.440
Is there a microphone running around?

01:05:58.360 --> 01:06:00.320
My question's for reality winner

01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:02.800
and I just wanna say thank you very much

01:06:02.800 --> 01:06:05.040
for everything you've done for everybody in the world

01:06:05.040 --> 01:06:07.920
and I find you extremely moving

01:06:07.920 --> 01:06:10.560
and I'm born in 1985 so also on behalf

01:06:10.560 --> 01:06:12.680
of our generation I say thank you very much

01:06:12.680 --> 01:06:14.400
and those who are coming next

01:06:15.600 --> 01:06:17.760
and also I would like to pre-curse my question

01:06:17.760 --> 01:06:20.920
by saying I talk a lot in my private messages

01:06:20.920 --> 01:06:22.520
with friends about murdering people

01:06:22.520 --> 01:06:25.400
which I think I will now stop doing

01:06:25.400 --> 01:06:28.160
but I have no intention to murder any of them.

01:06:28.160 --> 01:06:30.280
Yes, yeah, just also to be clear

01:06:30.280 --> 01:06:33.600
but I'm wondering my question isn't maybe not

01:06:33.600 --> 01:06:34.920
it's not so much about the film

01:06:34.920 --> 01:06:37.120
but I'd like to know about your pets

01:06:37.120 --> 01:06:39.280
and what your pet status is now.

01:06:43.580 --> 01:06:44.420
Did you hear that already?

01:06:44.420 --> 01:06:47.620
So yes, I heard it, yes.

01:06:48.540 --> 01:06:51.220
When it comes to animals our Facebook status is

01:06:51.220 --> 01:06:55.500
it's complicated, we have four dogs, three cats

01:06:55.500 --> 01:07:00.060
and a horse but the horse identifies as a dog.

01:07:00.060 --> 01:07:01.580
That's why it's complicated.

01:07:01.580 --> 01:07:05.620
He will run up on you, he barks at you,

01:07:05.620 --> 01:07:07.580
we got him a nice bala hay

01:07:07.580 --> 01:07:09.900
and he has destroyed it in less than a week

01:07:11.540 --> 01:07:14.820
but the dogs are also extremely high maintenance.

01:07:14.820 --> 01:07:18.780
They need certain dogs like to fight pretty bad

01:07:18.780 --> 01:07:20.780
so they need to be kept separate

01:07:20.780 --> 01:07:22.460
except when they're super sleepy

01:07:22.460 --> 01:07:23.700
and then they wanna cuddle.

01:07:23.700 --> 01:07:27.220
So you just never know, it's completely bipolar.

01:07:27.220 --> 01:07:30.220
Now that I have a job in the local community

01:07:31.540 --> 01:07:34.500
I am actually having like mom fears

01:07:34.500 --> 01:07:36.460
about leaving them home alone

01:07:36.460 --> 01:07:38.900
though I have like these contingency plans

01:07:38.900 --> 01:07:41.900
of who goes where and if the weather is bad

01:07:41.900 --> 01:07:44.140
who stays outside but who stays inside

01:07:44.140 --> 01:07:45.700
and maybe we can rotate.

01:07:46.700 --> 01:07:51.700
So yes, the four dogs are Domino, Daisy, Babyface

01:07:52.460 --> 01:07:55.060
and Dobby, the house self.

01:07:55.060 --> 01:07:56.460
The horse's name is Trouble

01:07:56.460 --> 01:07:58.340
because he's nothing but Trouble

01:07:58.340 --> 01:08:00.060
and then the cats are just irrelevant.

01:08:00.060 --> 01:08:01.580
They pretty much self maintain

01:08:01.580 --> 01:08:07.290
unless Fiona the princess likes to scream at us.

01:08:07.290 --> 01:08:10.410
That is quite a crew you have at your house, Billy.

01:08:12.650 --> 01:08:14.650
Are there other questions?

01:08:14.650 --> 01:08:15.490
Say again.

01:08:16.610 --> 01:08:20.530
I said the spiders are actually another situation.

01:08:20.530 --> 01:08:22.010
There will be giant ones

01:08:22.010 --> 01:08:25.370
like borderline tarantulas in the mailbox

01:08:25.370 --> 01:08:27.010
but I'm not allowed to remove them

01:08:27.010 --> 01:08:29.490
because my parents like to foster them.

01:08:29.490 --> 01:08:30.330
Okay.

01:08:30.330 --> 01:08:32.250
So that is the situation here as well.

01:08:32.250 --> 01:08:33.250
Oh, it's snakes.

01:08:33.250 --> 01:08:34.250
Yeah, I come from Canada.

01:08:34.250 --> 01:08:35.090
I'm used to snakes.

01:08:35.090 --> 01:08:36.090
Do you have snakes?

01:08:37.570 --> 01:08:40.010
Yes, actually Sonya got to see our pet snake

01:08:40.010 --> 01:08:41.970
and she was here visiting one time.

01:08:43.610 --> 01:08:44.610
But these aren't pets.

01:08:45.370 --> 01:08:48.050
These are animals that live around you.

01:08:48.050 --> 01:08:51.050
Yeah, and sometimes come in and say hello.

01:08:51.050 --> 01:08:53.410
Okay, great, great.

01:08:53.410 --> 01:08:57.000
Are there other questions?

01:08:57.000 --> 01:09:06.310
Yes.

01:09:06.310 --> 01:09:09.990
First of all, thank you, reality

01:09:09.990 --> 01:09:13.790
for your great courage here in Berlin.

01:09:13.790 --> 01:09:18.030
The whole audience was frantic, impressed, moved

01:09:18.950 --> 01:09:21.710
and I think also thank you, Billy

01:09:21.710 --> 01:09:24.110
for encouraging your daughter

01:09:25.190 --> 01:09:27.950
really super power mom.

01:09:27.950 --> 01:09:30.510
And I think there was a big enthusiasm

01:09:30.510 --> 01:09:32.110
at the end of the movie

01:09:32.110 --> 01:09:35.830
and after hearing how you're treated now,

01:09:35.830 --> 01:09:38.510
reality, I think we are all sobered.

01:09:38.510 --> 01:09:41.430
And I think the atmosphere,

01:09:41.430 --> 01:09:44.470
I had this impression changed a little bit

01:09:44.470 --> 01:09:46.870
and we wish you all the best.

01:09:46.870 --> 01:09:48.910
And so as I said,

01:09:48.910 --> 01:09:51.910
after having watched this impressive documentary,

01:09:52.750 --> 01:09:54.950
we had the impression that it's maybe over

01:09:54.950 --> 01:09:57.150
but obviously we are naive

01:09:57.150 --> 01:10:01.030
and I'm just trying to process

01:10:01.030 --> 01:10:04.350
as we all, the irony.

01:10:04.350 --> 01:10:08.270
And I think the irony goes around terms

01:10:08.270 --> 01:10:13.270
like patriotism and shame and angst.

01:10:14.070 --> 01:10:15.910
And I think there would be a whole world

01:10:15.910 --> 01:10:20.710
to study about the reactions

01:10:20.710 --> 01:10:24.470
of the US government right now,

01:10:24.470 --> 01:10:26.630
actually under a Biden government,

01:10:26.630 --> 01:10:28.150
which we maybe here in Berlin,

01:10:28.150 --> 01:10:29.470
we would be so naive to think

01:10:29.470 --> 01:10:33.070
that it would be all reverted to another angle.

01:10:33.070 --> 01:10:37.870
And if you allow me to say from my background,

01:10:37.870 --> 01:10:39.550
I don't know if it's of importance,

01:10:39.550 --> 01:10:41.670
but I just cannot not mention it.

01:10:42.870 --> 01:10:45.710
Next to art history, I studied Russian literature

01:10:45.710 --> 01:10:49.590
and I was a lot busy

01:10:49.590 --> 01:10:54.390
with the Soviet Union's oppressive system

01:10:54.390 --> 01:10:58.830
and following and shame and patriotism

01:10:58.830 --> 01:11:03.310
and being patronized and the whole psychosis

01:11:03.310 --> 01:11:07.390
over condemned people,

01:11:07.390 --> 01:11:09.310
not only in the 1920s century,

01:11:09.310 --> 01:11:12.190
but maybe even currently.

01:11:12.190 --> 01:11:17.190
So I think it's an irony of patriotism.

01:11:18.350 --> 01:11:23.270
So I think there's a comparison possible to do

01:11:23.270 --> 01:11:26.190
in this point, which is the biggest irony

01:11:26.190 --> 01:11:28.430
when we look at the case,

01:11:28.430 --> 01:11:30.910
when it's about Russia or the US.

01:11:30.910 --> 01:11:33.950
So maybe there is a bigger theme going on

01:11:33.950 --> 01:11:37.910
thinking about how a nation could defend patriotism

01:11:37.910 --> 01:11:39.830
or should speak up.

01:11:39.870 --> 01:11:41.750
So maybe at the end, maybe Sonya,

01:11:41.750 --> 01:11:45.070
I would like after beyond thanking you

01:11:45.070 --> 01:11:47.670
very much for this outstanding documentary,

01:11:47.670 --> 01:11:51.710
would you plan to cover in the future the story

01:11:51.710 --> 01:11:55.030
and help providing information?

01:11:55.030 --> 01:11:56.710
And sorry, I spoke too long,

01:11:56.710 --> 01:11:58.550
but I just wanted to get this out

01:11:58.550 --> 01:12:00.790
and thank you so much, everyone.

01:12:00.790 --> 01:12:01.630
Thank you.

01:12:01.630 --> 01:12:04.290
Would you like to comment at all?

01:12:04.290 --> 01:12:05.130
I'm not sure.

01:12:05.130 --> 01:12:07.650
Like if I want to continue covering the story or...

01:12:07.650 --> 01:12:09.010
Yeah, I guess that's good.

01:12:11.250 --> 01:12:14.850
I'm definitely still following it.

01:12:14.850 --> 01:12:17.570
And for independent filmmakers,

01:12:17.570 --> 01:12:20.290
I think films do not end.

01:12:21.810 --> 01:12:23.930
At least for me, they don't.

01:12:23.930 --> 01:12:28.930
I'm actually still very close also to the lead characters,

01:12:29.530 --> 01:12:30.970
the whistleblowers of National Bird,

01:12:30.970 --> 01:12:33.170
the drone war documentary.

01:12:33.170 --> 01:12:36.490
And I know we talked about Daniel Hale briefly earlier,

01:12:36.490 --> 01:12:40.930
but he is still in prison.

01:12:40.930 --> 01:12:45.930
And he did get a shorter sentence,

01:12:46.490 --> 01:12:49.410
but he had also prior to the sentence

01:12:49.410 --> 01:12:54.410
had many, many years of the sort of Damocles over him.

01:12:54.410 --> 01:12:57.810
And that's the issue with the Espionage Act

01:12:57.810 --> 01:13:02.010
that they were able to indict him

01:13:02.010 --> 01:13:04.650
so many years after his raid.

01:13:04.650 --> 01:13:08.450
And he didn't know when or if it would end.

01:13:08.490 --> 01:13:12.530
And then the other thing why I'm so passionate

01:13:12.530 --> 01:13:16.210
about bringing this information out about the Espionage Act

01:13:16.210 --> 01:13:20.570
is that I have seen when I was investigating other cases

01:13:20.570 --> 01:13:23.810
of not just whistleblowers, but also leakers,

01:13:23.810 --> 01:13:27.450
is that they are not all treated the same under the law.

01:13:27.450 --> 01:13:31.970
And that is what I as a journalist can really

01:13:31.970 --> 01:13:33.610
comment on very strongly.

01:13:33.610 --> 01:13:35.850
It's been applied very arbitrarily

01:13:35.970 --> 01:13:38.410
and people like General Petraeus

01:13:38.410 --> 01:13:41.530
have gotten away with a slap on the wrist and many others.

01:13:41.530 --> 01:13:44.850
And that's what I know Billy feels very passionately

01:13:44.850 --> 01:13:49.850
about as well, is that people are treated very differently

01:13:50.050 --> 01:13:52.130
and there are different types of laws,

01:13:52.130 --> 01:13:54.410
mishandling of classified information,

01:13:54.410 --> 01:13:56.410
misuse of a government computer

01:13:56.410 --> 01:13:59.530
that you could use instead of the Espionage Act,

01:13:59.530 --> 01:14:02.370
but they do use the Espionage Act

01:14:02.370 --> 01:14:05.250
particularly against national security whistleblowers.

01:14:06.730 --> 01:14:11.730
I think that came out a lot in just some of your voice

01:14:13.410 --> 01:14:15.930
in the documentary about this unknown

01:14:15.930 --> 01:14:19.010
that you had to live with, the unknowns.

01:14:19.010 --> 01:14:23.530
And even once you had had your plea deal arranged,

01:14:23.530 --> 01:14:26.650
you were looking at, as you said, no strings attached.

01:14:26.650 --> 01:14:28.090
I'm not sure if that felt better

01:14:28.090 --> 01:14:31.170
to know sort of what the parameters were

01:14:31.170 --> 01:14:35.010
or if it still felt like an unknown to you.

01:14:35.010 --> 01:14:37.050
Is that sort of what you find the hardest

01:14:37.050 --> 01:14:38.890
is just living with things

01:14:38.890 --> 01:14:43.170
that you don't really have control over?

01:14:43.170 --> 01:14:45.970
That is absolutely what this is,

01:14:45.970 --> 01:14:48.530
is the parameters of my plea deal

01:14:48.530 --> 01:14:50.570
are actually incredibly vague

01:14:50.570 --> 01:14:55.210
and they don't actually list what the repercussions

01:14:55.210 --> 01:15:00.210
are legally for even coming close to this line

01:15:01.130 --> 01:15:03.210
that's like a mile thick.

01:15:03.810 --> 01:15:07.850
You know, it's almost, like I said,

01:15:07.850 --> 01:15:11.050
my probation officer is looking at the same conditions

01:15:11.050 --> 01:15:15.450
that I've had legal scholars looking at for the past year

01:15:15.450 --> 01:15:16.930
to prepare for this time

01:15:16.930 --> 01:15:21.090
that I'm no longer in the department or the Bureau of Prisons.

01:15:22.330 --> 01:15:24.970
And somehow he reads all these lines

01:15:24.970 --> 01:15:27.890
and his summation is no interviews.

01:15:30.130 --> 01:15:32.170
Does that mean I can't do an interview

01:15:32.210 --> 01:15:34.210
about CrossFit?

01:15:34.210 --> 01:15:35.330
I'm a CrossFit coach.

01:15:35.330 --> 01:15:37.490
Why can't I talk about CrossFit?

01:15:37.490 --> 01:15:41.290
Why can't I be a public spokesperson for rescue horses?

01:15:43.010 --> 01:15:44.810
He doesn't seem to understand that.

01:15:46.290 --> 01:15:48.370
But the ball is in his court

01:15:49.690 --> 01:15:54.090
because there's no restrictions on what he can do to me

01:15:54.090 --> 01:15:57.370
if he can remand me and to custody it at any point.

01:15:57.370 --> 01:16:00.490
And because we can't seem to get my own country

01:16:00.490 --> 01:16:03.090
to pay attention to what's happening to me.

01:16:03.090 --> 01:16:07.010
Who knows how long it'll be before I can get released.

01:16:07.010 --> 01:16:10.850
There's not gonna be any public support or public pressure

01:16:10.850 --> 01:16:12.290
like in high profile cases.

01:16:12.290 --> 01:16:13.970
Nobody's coming to help me out.

01:16:14.850 --> 01:16:16.210
There's not gonna be any justice.

01:16:16.210 --> 01:16:18.530
It'll just be being silenced all over again

01:16:18.530 --> 01:16:21.330
and being alone and being in conditions

01:16:22.610 --> 01:16:25.610
where I can't manage my mental illness anymore.

01:16:25.610 --> 01:16:27.170
That's what I face every day

01:16:27.170 --> 01:16:29.410
because they change the rules every day.

01:16:31.050 --> 01:16:34.050
Billy, this sort of leads back to what you said

01:16:34.050 --> 01:16:37.250
I think at the very beginning.

01:16:37.250 --> 01:16:40.290
And it was something I think that seemed to hit you

01:16:40.290 --> 01:16:42.890
that you needed to be your daughter's voice.

01:16:42.890 --> 01:16:45.770
The first interviews that you were having,

01:16:45.770 --> 01:16:48.330
Gary spoke and you spoke and you went inside.

01:16:48.330 --> 01:16:51.410
You were trying not to be the main part of it.

01:16:51.410 --> 01:16:53.690
You were upset and you wanted to talk about it.

01:16:53.690 --> 01:16:56.010
But after a while, I think it was dawning on you

01:16:56.010 --> 01:17:00.050
that you needed to be the person talking to the media.

01:17:00.690 --> 01:17:03.650
And it brings me to that idea of your advocacy

01:17:03.650 --> 01:17:04.770
and the public narrative.

01:17:04.770 --> 01:17:06.730
Do you wanna talk a little bit about

01:17:06.730 --> 01:17:09.010
how you go about changing that public narrative

01:17:09.010 --> 01:17:12.890
or what's the value of it is in cases like realities?

01:17:14.690 --> 01:17:19.690
Well, the value of what I've done these last four years

01:17:20.290 --> 01:17:24.410
as far as being the spokesperson and speaking out

01:17:24.410 --> 01:17:28.890
is to make sure that the system knows

01:17:28.890 --> 01:17:32.170
that there are people out there who care

01:17:32.170 --> 01:17:36.450
so that they can't abuse reality further.

01:17:37.370 --> 01:17:41.370
My goal was to always make sure that there were eyes on her,

01:17:41.370 --> 01:17:44.570
that there were eyes on the case and the situation.

01:17:44.570 --> 01:17:48.170
And so that because if the system thinks

01:17:48.170 --> 01:17:49.770
that nobody's watching,

01:17:49.770 --> 01:17:52.970
that's when the system will abuse people.

01:17:52.970 --> 01:17:55.050
You see it time and time again.

01:17:55.050 --> 01:17:58.690
And so nothing, I know the Washington Post there,

01:17:58.690 --> 01:18:02.650
big mantra is nothing good happens in silence or darkness.

01:18:02.650 --> 01:18:04.690
And so that's kind of what I wanted to do

01:18:04.690 --> 01:18:07.490
was make sure that there was not this darkness

01:18:07.490 --> 01:18:10.530
around my daughter's case, there was not this silence.

01:18:10.530 --> 01:18:14.770
And that since they did a really good job of silencing her

01:18:14.770 --> 01:18:18.610
and also everyone involved in the legal case,

01:18:18.610 --> 01:18:20.410
there was this protective order,

01:18:20.410 --> 01:18:22.570
which in effect is a gag order.

01:18:23.970 --> 01:18:26.370
Nobody could talk about it.

01:18:26.370 --> 01:18:29.730
Somebody had to keep this case alive out there

01:18:29.730 --> 01:18:32.370
on social media and in the media.

01:18:32.370 --> 01:18:34.370
Somebody had to keep talking about it.

01:18:34.370 --> 01:18:38.250
And that was what I felt like my role was

01:18:38.250 --> 01:18:42.290
with the small group of supporters that I had

01:18:42.290 --> 01:18:43.850
was to keep this alive.

01:18:44.850 --> 01:18:46.890
Yeah, and Sonia, did you want to comment on that?

01:18:46.890 --> 01:18:51.170
Because you by your seeing what needed to be done,

01:18:51.170 --> 01:18:54.450
I think you've helped that go forward.

01:18:54.450 --> 01:18:56.450
And I hope this is the beginning again,

01:18:56.450 --> 01:19:01.450
a new beginning of keeping the light shone on this case

01:19:01.450 --> 01:19:04.010
and on reality in Billy's lives.

01:19:04.010 --> 01:19:06.650
Yeah, I just really hope anyone, the audience here

01:19:06.650 --> 01:19:11.650
who felt moved by the film and reality winners case

01:19:11.690 --> 01:19:13.610
especially the people who might have not heard

01:19:13.610 --> 01:19:17.130
about reality winner before, just spread the word.

01:19:17.130 --> 01:19:20.370
This is an independent film and production

01:19:20.370 --> 01:19:23.530
and we really rely on word of mouth

01:19:23.530 --> 01:19:28.530
to get it out there and share it as much as you can

01:19:30.730 --> 01:19:35.130
with your networks because I do think that people

01:19:35.130 --> 01:19:40.130
have to know about reality's story and also Billy's story.

01:19:42.170 --> 01:19:46.090
I think that's a great time to stop, but I would...

01:19:46.090 --> 01:19:49.010
Oh, there's a question from Tatiana.

01:19:49.010 --> 01:19:51.410
We still have time, but yes, sorry.

01:19:51.410 --> 01:19:56.410
Yes, I wanted to ask either to Billy or reality also,

01:19:57.410 --> 01:20:02.410
who can and won't speak about the role of the intercept

01:20:04.130 --> 01:20:07.690
because I think that was a really big point in the film

01:20:07.690 --> 01:20:11.130
and also a big point in the story of reality.

01:20:11.130 --> 01:20:13.650
Then in a sense, they burn the story

01:20:13.650 --> 01:20:17.210
before it actually even came to the public.

01:20:17.210 --> 01:20:21.250
And I think that this is a responsibility of the media

01:20:21.250 --> 01:20:25.450
to protect the sources and also to make possible

01:20:25.450 --> 01:20:29.930
that there is a story to speak about them

01:20:29.930 --> 01:20:33.410
that then the press can refer to

01:20:33.410 --> 01:20:36.890
and in the sense the person can be protected

01:20:36.890 --> 01:20:39.530
because this become public opinion.

01:20:39.530 --> 01:20:42.050
And for example, in the book,

01:20:42.050 --> 01:20:44.890
I'm doing an interview with Laura Poitras

01:20:44.890 --> 01:20:46.730
and she really speaks about that

01:20:46.730 --> 01:20:49.690
and also the responsibility of the intercept

01:20:49.970 --> 01:20:54.410
in actually burning the story before it came to the public.

01:20:55.410 --> 01:20:59.530
And so I also wanted to know if you can comment on that

01:20:59.530 --> 01:21:04.050
because I think we have also to openly discuss

01:21:04.050 --> 01:21:06.210
about this kind of failure

01:21:06.210 --> 01:21:09.330
because there was also a failure of the press.

01:21:09.330 --> 01:21:12.450
And so I think it's really important that at the moment

01:21:12.450 --> 01:21:16.010
to reflect on how the press can help you

01:21:16.010 --> 01:21:19.370
and not really silence your case even further.

01:21:22.260 --> 01:21:26.020
Do either of you reality or Billy want to make a comment?

01:21:26.020 --> 01:21:29.220
Because I know John would have a lot to say.

01:21:29.220 --> 01:21:33.610
I'll comment if you don't want to, but go ahead.

01:21:33.610 --> 01:21:36.850
I would like to say that there's a very disturbing trend

01:21:36.850 --> 01:21:39.250
and I know that journalists are aware of it

01:21:39.250 --> 01:21:43.130
but in any sort of corporate media enterprise,

01:21:43.130 --> 01:21:48.130
it becomes kind of corrupting in a way negative headline cell.

01:21:48.170 --> 01:21:53.170
Negative headline cell, no matter what the facts are,

01:21:53.450 --> 01:21:55.610
having a negative spin on it,

01:21:55.610 --> 01:22:00.610
more so than a positive spin is far more lucrative.

01:22:00.930 --> 01:22:04.050
And when a story isn't lucrative enough,

01:22:04.050 --> 01:22:06.730
they find a way to make it more negative.

01:22:06.730 --> 01:22:09.770
So in my case, it was a calculated move.

01:22:09.770 --> 01:22:11.870
It wasn't a mistake.

01:22:11.870 --> 01:22:14.810
They needed a martyr because it was more lucrative

01:22:14.810 --> 01:22:18.010
and that's why they've repeatedly burned sources

01:22:18.010 --> 01:22:21.730
because it's easier to champion someone

01:22:23.170 --> 01:22:27.170
in a story that's overwhelmingly negative,

01:22:27.170 --> 01:22:32.170
even if it's a manufactured sort of incident.

01:22:34.170 --> 01:22:35.810
So they needed someone to have the fall

01:22:35.810 --> 01:22:38.050
to make that information more lucrative

01:22:38.050 --> 01:22:43.510
as a journalistic enterprise and corporate media.

01:22:43.510 --> 01:22:44.790
And I paid the price.

01:22:45.790 --> 01:22:48.790
And I wondered just as I was watching

01:22:48.790 --> 01:22:55.320
if the fact that the story that the source

01:22:55.480 --> 01:22:57.560
hadn't been protected also made the media

01:22:57.560 --> 01:23:00.640
not really want to delve much into the story

01:23:00.640 --> 01:23:03.200
because it was a story about a media failure

01:23:03.200 --> 01:23:05.560
if they really were looking closely enough.

01:23:07.200 --> 01:23:10.680
I can add a couple of things to intercept too.

01:23:12.400 --> 01:23:15.040
Matthew Cole and Richard Esposito,

01:23:15.040 --> 01:23:17.220
two of the journalists that were responsible

01:23:17.220 --> 01:23:20.960
for essentially outing reality, also outed me.

01:23:22.000 --> 01:23:25.800
I got an email one time from Matthew Cole

01:23:25.800 --> 01:23:29.120
and it contained a dozen names.

01:23:29.120 --> 01:23:32.860
And he said, hey, I'm writing a book about this rendition.

01:23:32.860 --> 01:23:35.760
Can you introduce me to any of these 12 people?

01:23:35.760 --> 01:23:38.480
And I responded, I don't know who these people are.

01:23:38.480 --> 01:23:41.240
Kidnappings weren't my thing at the CIA.

01:23:41.240 --> 01:23:43.160
I can't help you.

01:23:43.160 --> 01:23:46.840
And he sent me a second email with another 12 names.

01:23:46.840 --> 01:23:50.080
And I said, you clearly know this issue better than I do.

01:23:50.080 --> 01:23:52.960
I don't know who any of these people are.

01:23:52.960 --> 01:23:56.240
And he said in a third email, what about the guy

01:23:56.240 --> 01:24:00.240
that you mentioned on page 100 and something

01:24:00.240 --> 01:24:03.840
of your book, I think his name is John.

01:24:04.860 --> 01:24:09.860
And I said, oh, you mean John Doe.

01:24:10.120 --> 01:24:12.120
I said, I don't know whatever happened to him.

01:24:12.120 --> 01:24:18.250
He's probably retired and living in Virginia somewhere.

01:24:18.250 --> 01:24:19.490
I shouldn't have said the name.

01:24:19.490 --> 01:24:24.490
I confirmed the last name that I'm calling Doe right now.

01:24:25.930 --> 01:24:29.090
Well, Matthew Cole wasn't working for,

01:24:29.090 --> 01:24:31.250
he wasn't doing this as a book.

01:24:31.250 --> 01:24:32.550
There was no book.

01:24:32.550 --> 01:24:33.690
It was a cover story.

01:24:33.690 --> 01:24:34.530
It was a lie.

01:24:34.530 --> 01:24:37.090
He was secretly working for the Guantanamo defense

01:24:37.090 --> 01:24:38.690
attorneys.

01:24:38.690 --> 01:24:41.530
So he had collected these 24 names.

01:24:41.530 --> 01:24:45.410
I had confirmed the 25th and he sent all these names

01:24:45.410 --> 01:24:46.890
to Guantanamo.

01:24:46.890 --> 01:24:50.890
The attorneys there put the names into a classified motion

01:24:53.890 --> 01:24:58.330
and asked the judge to demand that they be interviewed.

01:24:58.330 --> 01:25:01.150
The judge realized that these names were all classified.

01:25:01.150 --> 01:25:03.530
So he gave the names to the FBI.

01:25:03.530 --> 01:25:05.730
The FBI went to the defense attorneys

01:25:05.730 --> 01:25:08.170
and they said, where did you get the names?

01:25:08.170 --> 01:25:11.010
They said from John Shipton, an investigator

01:25:11.010 --> 01:25:12.290
for Human Rights Watch.

01:25:12.290 --> 01:25:13.650
So they went to Shipton.

01:25:13.650 --> 01:25:15.210
Where did you get the names?

01:25:15.210 --> 01:25:16.890
From Matthew Cole.

01:25:16.890 --> 01:25:17.970
So they went to Cole.

01:25:17.970 --> 01:25:19.250
Where did you get the names?

01:25:19.250 --> 01:25:21.770
Now, this is a journalist, mind you.

01:25:21.770 --> 01:25:25.880
He said, I got him from John Kiriakou.

01:25:25.880 --> 01:25:28.040
Then they convened a grand jury

01:25:28.040 --> 01:25:30.040
and they called Matthew Cole.

01:25:30.040 --> 01:25:30.920
Where did you get the names?

01:25:30.920 --> 01:25:32.720
John Kiriakou gave me the name.

01:25:34.080 --> 01:25:37.920
So they charged me with five felonies,

01:25:37.960 --> 01:25:40.320
including three counts of espionage,

01:25:40.320 --> 01:25:43.080
45 years in prison,

01:25:43.080 --> 01:25:47.840
because Matthew Cole either was afraid,

01:25:47.840 --> 01:25:51.440
feared for his own liability,

01:25:51.440 --> 01:25:54.240
or he was working for the FBI,

01:25:55.120 --> 01:25:57.280
which I've also come to believe is true.

01:25:57.280 --> 01:25:59.060
Because it wasn't just me.

01:25:59.060 --> 01:26:01.440
It wasn't just me and reality.

01:26:01.440 --> 01:26:04.080
He did the same thing to an FBI whistleblower,

01:26:04.080 --> 01:26:05.920
Terry Albury.

01:26:05.920 --> 01:26:08.120
He outed Terry Albury to the FBI

01:26:08.120 --> 01:26:10.800
and Terry Albury did three and a half years in prison.

01:26:12.040 --> 01:26:15.760
You know, and they've done the same thing to Daniel Hale.

01:26:16.760 --> 01:26:17.720
Blower.

01:26:17.720 --> 01:26:19.640
Daniel Hale provided his information.

01:26:21.200 --> 01:26:23.920
You know, the FBI's raiding his house

01:26:23.920 --> 01:26:30.810
and he's getting four.

01:26:30.810 --> 01:26:33.930
My brain can't process the notion

01:26:35.210 --> 01:26:38.450
they are so stupid

01:26:38.450 --> 01:26:42.050
or such bad journalists

01:26:42.050 --> 01:26:44.090
that they keep making the same mistake

01:26:44.090 --> 01:26:46.010
over and over and over.

01:26:46.010 --> 01:26:47.690
I think reality's right.

01:26:47.690 --> 01:26:49.210
They do it for the headlines,

01:26:49.210 --> 01:26:50.490
but I'm more cynical

01:26:50.490 --> 01:26:53.170
and I think they're working for the FBI.

01:26:53.170 --> 01:26:57.450
I really do.

01:26:57.450 --> 01:27:00.850
That's not a good, sorry.

01:27:00.850 --> 01:27:02.010
There's a microphone issue.

01:27:02.010 --> 01:27:05.130
If I could add something to that.

01:27:05.130 --> 01:27:07.610
Sorry, Billy, did you want to jump in there?

01:27:08.610 --> 01:27:12.050
I just also wanted to add throughout this,

01:27:12.050 --> 01:27:17.050
I've always looked back at when the intercept

01:27:17.130 --> 01:27:21.290
published the document that reality released.

01:27:21.290 --> 01:27:24.010
They published it after her arrest.

01:27:24.010 --> 01:27:28.170
They published it after her court hearing.

01:27:28.170 --> 01:27:30.970
They had an agreement with the government

01:27:30.970 --> 01:27:35.970
to hold off on the story until after her arrest.

01:27:36.290 --> 01:27:40.610
When is it that a reputable journalist

01:27:40.610 --> 01:27:44.770
or media source actually has an agreement

01:27:44.770 --> 01:27:49.520
with the government on things like this?

01:27:49.520 --> 01:27:54.800
Yeah, no, that sounds, there is a problem.

01:27:54.800 --> 01:27:56.800
And I do think one of the things it raises,

01:27:56.800 --> 01:27:58.280
whether there's a specific problem

01:27:58.280 --> 01:28:03.080
with specific journalists and a specific organization,

01:28:03.080 --> 01:28:06.560
there is a problem with, I think,

01:28:06.600 --> 01:28:11.680
the self-censorship, the not wanting to touch the stories,

01:28:11.680 --> 01:28:15.520
the issue of actually doing what you can.

01:28:15.520 --> 01:28:20.520
Obviously, it is an arms race between investigative media

01:28:22.000 --> 01:28:23.920
and some of these independent media

01:28:23.920 --> 01:28:27.240
and the NSA and the whistleblowers.

01:28:27.240 --> 01:28:32.240
And a lot of the power is we know where it sits.

01:28:32.480 --> 01:28:35.280
And a lot of the idea that you're going to engage

01:28:35.320 --> 01:28:38.040
in that battle and win is not easy.

01:28:38.040 --> 01:28:43.040
So you need to, but the issue of journalism

01:28:43.400 --> 01:28:47.040
and doing it well and doing it properly

01:28:47.040 --> 01:28:49.560
has to be at the basis of whistleblowers

01:28:49.560 --> 01:28:51.280
going to journalists.

01:28:51.280 --> 01:28:55.000
And we can see that there are plenty of organizations

01:28:55.000 --> 01:28:58.400
being set up outside of, and Intercept was one of them,

01:28:59.280 --> 01:29:01.280
outside of the traditional media

01:29:01.280 --> 01:29:03.400
to address some of these issues.

01:29:03.440 --> 01:29:07.480
And right now, obviously, we also have the Espionage Act

01:29:07.480 --> 01:29:11.800
being used against Julian Assange, a publisher,

01:29:11.800 --> 01:29:14.400
and used transatlantically.

01:29:14.400 --> 01:29:17.280
And the impact and the idea of how the Espionage

01:29:17.280 --> 01:29:20.280
is going to, Espionage Act is going to continue

01:29:20.280 --> 01:29:23.600
to affect journalists doing their jobs well

01:29:23.600 --> 01:29:25.920
and properly in the public interest

01:29:25.920 --> 01:29:28.760
is obviously not going to go away.

01:29:28.760 --> 01:29:30.320
Sonia or John, would you?

01:29:30.320 --> 01:29:31.920
May I add one thing to that?

01:29:32.920 --> 01:29:37.080
There's a fantastic journalist and a friend of whistleblowers

01:29:37.080 --> 01:29:41.280
by the name of, it's going to come to me in a second.

01:29:41.280 --> 01:29:44.480
He's at BuzzFeed, Jason Leopold at BuzzFeed.

01:29:44.480 --> 01:29:47.040
He's the king of the Freedom of Information Act.

01:29:47.040 --> 01:29:49.560
In fact, a senior defense department official

01:29:49.560 --> 01:29:53.160
called him a FOIA terrorist because he's uncovered

01:29:53.160 --> 01:29:56.440
so much information about government wrongdoing

01:29:56.440 --> 01:29:57.880
through the Freedom of Information Act

01:29:57.880 --> 01:29:59.760
that they fear him now.

01:29:59.760 --> 01:30:02.680
But anyway, he sent a Freedom of Information Act

01:30:02.680 --> 01:30:07.680
request to the CIA about two years ago just on a lark.

01:30:08.200 --> 01:30:13.200
And he asked for all communication between all journalists

01:30:14.400 --> 01:30:17.520
and the CIA's Office of Public Affairs.

01:30:17.520 --> 01:30:20.440
And they sent him thousands and thousands of pages

01:30:20.440 --> 01:30:25.440
of just boring, useless, oh, I have a question.

01:30:26.320 --> 01:30:28.400
What's the CIA director's birthday

01:30:28.400 --> 01:30:31.240
and silly stuff like that?

01:30:31.240 --> 01:30:33.760
But then he found a golden nugget.

01:30:35.040 --> 01:30:38.520
Ken Delanian, the senior intelligence reporter

01:30:38.520 --> 01:30:43.520
for NBC News and MSNBC, had been sending his articles

01:30:45.560 --> 01:30:49.740
to the CIA for clearance before he sent them

01:30:49.740 --> 01:30:51.560
to his own editors.

01:30:53.000 --> 01:30:53.840
Why?

01:30:53.840 --> 01:30:56.080
Why would he do something like that

01:30:56.120 --> 01:31:01.120
if he's not putting CIA planted stories in the news?

01:31:03.080 --> 01:31:07.320
It's because when you're a national security journalist

01:31:07.320 --> 01:31:11.240
in Washington, it's a big deal to get invited

01:31:11.240 --> 01:31:13.940
to the CIA Christmas party, right?

01:31:13.940 --> 01:31:15.920
You get to shake the director's hand,

01:31:15.920 --> 01:31:18.000
they'll let you go into the little souvenir store

01:31:18.000 --> 01:31:20.560
and buy a CIA tie.

01:31:20.560 --> 01:31:21.520
I'm serious.

01:31:22.640 --> 01:31:25.440
And if you say something in your publication

01:31:25.440 --> 01:31:27.800
or on your network that the CIA doesn't like,

01:31:27.800 --> 01:31:30.760
you're not invited to the Christmas party next year.

01:31:30.760 --> 01:31:34.120
And they're not gonna give you the little leak,

01:31:34.120 --> 01:31:36.400
the little information that they want to plant

01:31:36.400 --> 01:31:37.600
in the media.

01:31:37.600 --> 01:31:41.200
And they're not gonna call you with a tip anymore.

01:31:41.200 --> 01:31:42.720
They'll do all of those things

01:31:42.720 --> 01:31:46.060
if you do exactly as they tell you to do.

01:31:47.160 --> 01:31:49.520
And so that's what Ken Delanian was doing.

01:31:49.880 --> 01:31:54.880
He was cowtowing to the CIA

01:31:54.880 --> 01:31:57.480
to be on their good guys list.

01:31:57.480 --> 01:32:00.720
Now part of the problem is that most publications

01:32:00.720 --> 01:32:03.200
and networks in the United States no longer have a budget

01:32:03.200 --> 01:32:05.280
for investigative journalism.

01:32:05.280 --> 01:32:09.780
And so what they do is they take the CIA press releases

01:32:09.780 --> 01:32:13.320
or they take the cleared paragraphs

01:32:13.320 --> 01:32:16.360
that the CIA will send and they'll gist it

01:32:16.360 --> 01:32:20.080
and they'll add a paragraph that they pull off Wikipedia

01:32:20.080 --> 01:32:21.440
or wherever they find it.

01:32:21.440 --> 01:32:24.400
And that becomes a news story.

01:32:24.400 --> 01:32:27.440
But that's not news, that's propaganda.

01:32:28.320 --> 01:32:31.000
We used to have a law in the United States

01:32:31.000 --> 01:32:35.680
that forbade the propagandization of the American people.

01:32:35.680 --> 01:32:39.440
What most Americans don't know is that that law

01:32:39.440 --> 01:32:42.960
was revoked in 2011 as part

01:32:42.960 --> 01:32:45.480
of the National Defense Authorization Act.

01:32:45.480 --> 01:32:50.480
And so our news outlets now are legally permitted

01:32:52.080 --> 01:32:56.840
to publish CIA and FBI propaganda.

01:32:56.840 --> 01:32:59.200
There's nothing wrong with that anymore.

01:32:59.200 --> 01:33:02.520
And either Americans don't know or they don't care.

01:33:02.520 --> 01:33:03.920
I was just gonna throw a, you know,

01:33:03.920 --> 01:33:05.720
oh, that's what called balance, right?

01:33:05.720 --> 01:33:08.280
That's the giving each side there, say.

01:33:09.120 --> 01:33:12.280
Would you, yeah, yes.

01:33:12.280 --> 01:33:14.600
Would you like to comment on this issue?

01:33:14.640 --> 01:33:15.480
Oh, yeah.

01:33:16.760 --> 01:33:18.480
It's really very personal to me.

01:33:18.480 --> 01:33:21.120
I mean, yeah, the funding, of course,

01:33:21.120 --> 01:33:23.880
of investigative journalism is a problem

01:33:23.880 --> 01:33:25.920
because it's expensive, it takes time.

01:33:25.920 --> 01:33:29.480
You know, you saw at the beginning of the film

01:33:29.480 --> 01:33:32.280
we are opening with a text card that says

01:33:32.280 --> 01:33:37.280
that we were able to get the FBI interrogation audio

01:33:38.440 --> 01:33:41.960
through a lawsuit, but against the FBI,

01:33:42.000 --> 01:33:44.160
that was, you know, that started

01:33:44.160 --> 01:33:46.920
with a Freedom of Information Act request.

01:33:46.920 --> 01:33:50.360
Then after, you know, we have to give the FBI

01:33:50.360 --> 01:33:52.720
quite a lot of time for them to react

01:33:52.720 --> 01:33:56.160
because they put you on these like extremely long paths.

01:33:56.160 --> 01:33:58.560
And then when nothing happened

01:33:59.720 --> 01:34:01.320
and you know, we have to follow up

01:34:01.320 --> 01:34:02.160
and they rejected it.

01:34:02.160 --> 01:34:04.440
Then we went to the Department of Justice

01:34:04.440 --> 01:34:07.120
and made our argument why we thought

01:34:07.120 --> 01:34:10.760
we should get access to this material.

01:34:10.760 --> 01:34:12.960
And then their DOJ quite surprisingly

01:34:12.960 --> 01:34:14.200
actually sided with us.

01:34:14.200 --> 01:34:18.160
It was sent back to the FBI and they still didn't move.

01:34:18.160 --> 01:34:22.800
And at some point, you know, about one half years in

01:34:22.800 --> 01:34:26.280
we went to the Reporters Committee for Freedom of the Press

01:34:26.280 --> 01:34:28.240
and they provided pro bono support

01:34:28.240 --> 01:34:30.160
because as an independent team, you know,

01:34:30.160 --> 01:34:33.680
we cannot afford these type of legal expenses.

01:34:33.680 --> 01:34:37.400
So they represented us and we sued the FBI

01:34:37.840 --> 01:34:41.200
and it took almost two years, but we won.

01:34:41.200 --> 01:34:44.440
And we actually had fortunately a judge

01:34:44.440 --> 01:34:47.720
who sided with us when the FBI,

01:34:47.720 --> 01:34:49.120
I think I was calculating, they said

01:34:49.120 --> 01:34:51.520
it would take them 13 years or something

01:34:51.520 --> 01:34:54.640
to release the data because they wanted to chop up

01:34:54.640 --> 01:34:57.920
the audio into multiple smaller files

01:34:57.920 --> 01:34:59.200
and release them every month,

01:34:59.200 --> 01:35:02.040
which, you know, I know it takes a lot more time

01:35:02.040 --> 01:35:03.840
than just releasing the file to us.

01:35:03.840 --> 01:35:06.920
It already had been redacted.

01:35:06.920 --> 01:35:11.720
So yeah, we got that, but it really,

01:35:11.720 --> 01:35:14.640
it takes a lot of time and knowledge,

01:35:14.640 --> 01:35:18.240
but I wish that big media organizations,

01:35:18.240 --> 01:35:20.720
public media would really invest

01:35:20.720 --> 01:35:23.040
in this type of investigative research

01:35:23.040 --> 01:35:25.600
and not just, you know, a PR person, a press person

01:35:25.600 --> 01:35:28.040
of an agency, that's not a source.

01:35:28.040 --> 01:35:29.920
You know, if they give you information,

01:35:29.920 --> 01:35:33.360
that is not, that's like a placing information.

01:35:33.360 --> 01:35:35.600
That is not a source.

01:35:35.600 --> 01:35:39.000
But I think you can actually find a lot of information,

01:35:39.000 --> 01:35:41.000
like you mentioned with Jason Leopold,

01:35:41.000 --> 01:35:43.520
through, you know, reading court records,

01:35:43.520 --> 01:35:44.840
congressional budget reports.

01:35:44.840 --> 01:35:47.680
I was reading through so many congressional budget reports

01:35:47.680 --> 01:35:50.200
during the production of National Bird

01:35:50.200 --> 01:35:53.520
and found a lot of information about, you know,

01:35:53.520 --> 01:35:56.560
the drone program in these reports

01:35:56.560 --> 01:35:58.440
and court records and so on.

01:35:58.440 --> 01:36:01.200
And, but yes, it's dry work.

01:36:01.200 --> 01:36:03.280
It doesn't, it's not as flashy

01:36:03.280 --> 01:36:06.680
as having that, you know, new leak

01:36:06.680 --> 01:36:10.160
that you have of classified materials.

01:36:10.160 --> 01:36:13.840
So it's, you know, it really takes more time,

01:36:13.840 --> 01:36:18.640
but I do, I really hope that the funding will be provided,

01:36:18.640 --> 01:36:19.920
maybe by more foundations.

01:36:19.920 --> 01:36:22.680
I mean, I saw here, this is supported

01:36:22.680 --> 01:36:24.480
by every Van David Logan Foundation,

01:36:24.480 --> 01:36:29.000
which actually has been a big sponsor of my work as well

01:36:29.000 --> 01:36:31.560
and has made it able, possible for us

01:36:31.560 --> 01:36:34.320
to do this long-term research.

01:36:34.320 --> 01:36:36.480
But yeah, we need support.

01:36:36.480 --> 01:36:38.600
We probably need more, you know, public support.

01:36:38.600 --> 01:36:42.280
Maybe we have to go more to get funding from the people,

01:36:42.280 --> 01:36:46.920
but it's important because there's a lot of information hidden

01:36:46.920 --> 01:36:49.480
that is in the public interest.

01:36:49.480 --> 01:36:51.560
And I think Reality Winner's Case

01:36:51.560 --> 01:36:53.720
is one of the prime examples.

01:36:53.720 --> 01:36:56.320
What could be more important to the public

01:36:56.320 --> 01:36:58.200
than the security of our elections?

01:36:59.200 --> 01:37:00.240
Thank you, Sonia.

01:37:00.240 --> 01:37:10.720
I think that nicely brings us full circle

01:37:10.720 --> 01:37:15.720
because I was thinking about Billy writing about We the People

01:37:15.720 --> 01:37:18.240
and how your own belief in the American system

01:37:18.240 --> 01:37:25.240
has been tested beyond, beyond what you could live with,

01:37:25.240 --> 01:37:26.800
really, and that it's been destroyed.

01:37:26.800 --> 01:37:28.880
But it does bring us back to We the People

01:37:28.880 --> 01:37:33.720
because this event and everybody that's been involved in

01:37:34.320 --> 01:37:37.000
publishing the book, putting this all together,

01:37:37.000 --> 01:37:40.960
Reality, you taking that step to send that report.

01:37:40.960 --> 01:37:43.680
And, you know, we thank you for that.

01:37:43.680 --> 01:37:46.360
It does show where our accountability mechanisms are

01:37:46.360 --> 01:37:47.280
failing.

01:37:47.280 --> 01:37:49.400
You were trying to call that to account.

01:37:49.400 --> 01:37:53.720
It's up to us to take on the rest of it with you,

01:37:53.720 --> 01:37:55.680
but not leaving you to do it on your own

01:37:55.680 --> 01:37:57.760
or Billy on her own.

01:37:57.760 --> 01:38:01.360
So thank you so, so much for joining us today.

01:38:01.360 --> 01:38:03.000
It really is an honor for us.

01:38:03.000 --> 01:38:06.240
I don't know if you realize how much it has been

01:38:06.240 --> 01:38:09.800
and it is, despite, I realize a difficult period

01:38:09.800 --> 01:38:12.880
and it will take time and you will get more confident

01:38:12.880 --> 01:38:16.120
about what's going on with your probation officer

01:38:16.120 --> 01:38:17.480
and you'll hear from John.

01:38:19.000 --> 01:38:21.480
But it is really important to know that you're not alone

01:38:21.480 --> 01:38:25.360
and that we're out here trying to make this work better

01:38:25.360 --> 01:38:26.640
for all of us.

01:38:26.640 --> 01:38:29.720
So We the People, thank you.

01:38:31.000 --> 01:38:32.160
Thank all of you.

01:38:32.200 --> 01:38:54.400
Thank you.

01:38:54.400 --> 01:38:59.320
I also wanted to thank really deeply Reality and Billy

01:38:59.320 --> 01:39:01.720
for being with us this night.

01:39:01.720 --> 01:39:05.240
I hope you are also going to follow us tomorrow

01:39:05.240 --> 01:39:09.520
if you have time and you want to see how we go on here

01:39:09.520 --> 01:39:10.360
in Berlin.

01:39:11.360 --> 01:39:16.320
And I want to thank all the people in the panel,

01:39:16.320 --> 01:39:18.200
John, Sonia and Anna.

01:39:18.200 --> 01:39:21.040
This was really an important conversation.

01:39:21.080 --> 01:39:24.960
And really, I would say,

01:39:24.960 --> 01:39:27.920
we will keep thinking about your reality

01:39:27.920 --> 01:39:32.480
and also I hope that this event will also help

01:39:32.480 --> 01:39:36.080
in raising more interest and support for your case.

01:39:36.080 --> 01:39:38.760
So we are with you and we stand with you.

01:39:40.080 --> 01:39:44.440
I also then wanted to conclude the night of today

01:39:44.440 --> 01:39:47.680
to remind you to come back tomorrow.

01:39:47.680 --> 01:39:52.520
And briefly, I wanted to announce what is happening.

01:39:53.840 --> 01:39:58.320
So we start at four with the book launch.

01:39:58.320 --> 01:39:59.920
We're still blowing for change.

01:39:59.920 --> 01:40:03.920
So I will be here together with Elena Velenoska

01:40:03.920 --> 01:40:07.920
to speak more in depth about the work we did

01:40:07.920 --> 01:40:12.160
together with other sort of people that wrote in the book.

01:40:13.520 --> 01:40:16.760
And by the way, the book is here available

01:40:16.760 --> 01:40:20.720
if you want and also online on EPUB and PDF for free

01:40:20.720 --> 01:40:22.480
if you want to get it.

01:40:22.480 --> 01:40:25.880
And then after that, we will have a panel

01:40:25.880 --> 01:40:30.160
Crowdsourced Civic Action, subverting vigilance

01:40:30.160 --> 01:40:32.400
and powering whistleblowers.

01:40:32.400 --> 01:40:36.640
And together with me, there will be Barrett Brown,

01:40:36.640 --> 01:40:40.600
Naomi Colvin, Lori Love and Mustafa Al Bassem.

01:40:41.560 --> 01:40:45.360
And then we will have a second panel,

01:40:45.400 --> 01:40:48.320
challenging discrimination and polarization,

01:40:48.320 --> 01:40:51.400
whistleblowing the post-truth era,

01:40:51.400 --> 01:40:56.120
together with Darryl Davies and Imashon Robert Trafford

01:40:56.120 --> 01:40:58.000
of forensic architecture

01:40:58.000 --> 01:41:01.360
and is moderated by Peter Matiasic.

01:41:01.360 --> 01:41:03.040
I also want to remember

01:41:03.040 --> 01:41:06.400
that there are two workshops on Sunday

01:41:06.400 --> 01:41:10.280
that still have places if you want to attend.

01:41:10.280 --> 01:41:13.600
One is building secure whistleblowing platform

01:41:13.600 --> 01:41:16.200
with GlobalLeaks free software,

01:41:16.200 --> 01:41:18.800
with Rimas Gair of GlobalLeaks.

01:41:18.800 --> 01:41:21.880
And the other is two play or B-plades,

01:41:21.880 --> 01:41:26.880
the gamification workshop with Agnese Trocchi

01:41:26.880 --> 01:41:29.440
and Jacobo Anderlini.

01:41:29.440 --> 01:41:31.880
The two workshop will be offline

01:41:31.880 --> 01:41:35.480
and because of course it's also a matter of security

01:41:35.480 --> 01:41:37.480
and small participation.

01:41:37.480 --> 01:41:42.480
So I just remember again that you can just go online

01:41:42.600 --> 01:41:45.120
and get your ticket there.

01:41:45.120 --> 01:41:48.600
So this is it for today

01:41:48.600 --> 01:41:52.280
and I really want to thank you again for being with us

01:41:52.280 --> 01:41:54.760
and for this really important panel.

01:41:54.760 --> 01:42:17.710
Thank you and goodbye to reality and Billy, see you, bye.

